1
00:00:11,040 --> 00:00:12,420
So what'd you think?

2
00:00:12,420 --> 00:00:13,880
It was good.

3
00:00:13,880 --> 00:00:15,160
That's it?

4
00:00:15,160 --> 00:00:16,790
"Good"?

5
00:00:16,790 --> 00:00:18,330
I enjoyed it.

6
00:00:18,330 --> 00:00:20,720
When you told me I was going to be "losing my virginity,"

7
00:00:20,720 --> 00:00:21,880
I didn't think you meant showing me

8
00:00:21,880 --> 00:00:24,890
Raiders of the Lost Ark for the first time.

9
00:00:25,060 --> 00:00:28,250
My apologies. I chose my words poorly.

10
00:00:28,250 --> 00:00:29,740
I should have said you were about

11
00:00:29,740 --> 00:00:33,020
to have your world rocked on my couch.

12
00:00:34,470 --> 00:00:36,830
Anyway, thank you for watching it.

13
00:00:36,830 --> 00:00:38,960
It's one of my all-time favorites.

14
00:00:38,960 --> 00:00:40,600
It was very entertaining...

15
00:00:40,600 --> 00:00:43,800
despite the glaring story problem.

16
00:00:44,550 --> 00:00:46,080
Story problem?!

17
00:00:46,080 --> 00:00:49,230
You-- oh, Amy...

18
00:00:50,400 --> 00:00:53,510
What a dewy-eyed moon-calf you are.

19
00:00:53,510 --> 00:00:56,250
Raiders of the Lost Ark is the love child

20
00:00:56,250 --> 00:00:58,390
of Steven Spielberg and George Lucas,

21
00:00:58,400 --> 00:01:01,100
two of the most gifted filmmakers of our generation.

22
00:01:01,100 --> 00:01:03,570
I've watched it 36 times,

23
00:01:03,570 --> 00:01:06,910
except for the snake scene and the face-melting scene,

24
00:01:06,910 --> 00:01:10,340
which I can only watch when it's still light out, but...

25
00:01:10,340 --> 00:01:13,640
I defy you to find a story problem.

26
00:01:13,640 --> 00:01:14,920
Here's my jaw...

27
00:01:14,920 --> 00:01:16,690
drop it.

28
00:01:17,860 --> 00:01:19,110
All right.

29
00:01:19,110 --> 00:01:21,310
Indiana Jones plays no role

30
00:01:21,310 --> 00:01:22,970
in the outcome of the story.

31
00:01:22,970 --> 00:01:24,460
If he weren't in the film,

32
00:01:24,460 --> 00:01:27,100
it would turn out exactly the same.

33
00:01:27,100 --> 00:01:30,270
Oh, I see your confusion. You don't understand.

34
00:01:30,270 --> 00:01:34,660
Indiana Jones was the one in the hat with the whip.

35
00:01:35,240 --> 00:01:36,780
No, I do,

36
00:01:36,780 --> 00:01:38,280
and if he weren't in the movie,

37
00:01:38,280 --> 00:01:40,200
the Nazis would have still found the ark,

38
00:01:40,200 --> 00:01:43,390
taken it to the island, opened it up and all died...

39
00:01:43,390 --> 00:01:46,710
just like they did.

40
00:01:50,860 --> 00:01:53,040
Let me close that for ya.

41
00:02:22,590 --> 00:02:25,240
I thought you went to the comic book store on Wednesdays.

42
00:02:25,240 --> 00:02:27,870
Yeah, but Sheldon and Amy were having date night

43
00:02:27,870 --> 00:02:29,870
and they don't need me there to make it awkward.

44
00:02:31,450 --> 00:02:33,420
They have each other for that.

45
00:02:34,810 --> 00:02:35,900
So, how was school?

46
00:02:35,900 --> 00:02:37,580
Oh, good. Check it out.

47
00:02:37,580 --> 00:02:41,470
The Disappointing Child by Beverly Hofstadter.

48
00:02:50,130 --> 00:02:52,300
- You bought my mom's book? - Yeah!

49
00:02:53,130 --> 00:02:56,670
It's on the recommended reading list for my psychology class.

50
00:02:59,910 --> 00:03:02,340
Come on. Not that book.

51
00:03:02,340 --> 00:03:04,670
It-It's got, like, every horrible story

52
00:03:04,670 --> 00:03:07,030
from my childhood in it.

53
00:03:08,060 --> 00:03:10,530
Oh, cool. Are there pictures?

54
00:03:11,650 --> 00:03:13,980
Seriously, please find another book.

55
00:03:13,980 --> 00:03:16,300
Oh, come on. Why? How bad could it be?

56
00:03:16,300 --> 00:03:19,360
There-There's chapters about potty training,

57
00:03:19,360 --> 00:03:21,440
and bed-wetting and...

58
00:03:21,440 --> 00:03:24,020
masturbation.

59
00:03:25,350 --> 00:03:26,880
Basically, if something came out of me,

60
00:03:26,880 --> 00:03:29,080
she wrote about it!

61
00:03:30,390 --> 00:03:32,120
You know what? Do whatever you want,

62
00:03:32,120 --> 00:03:33,900
just don't talk to me about it.

63
00:03:33,900 --> 00:03:37,390
Not even the chapter on the breast-feeding crisis?

64
00:03:42,230 --> 00:03:45,000
It was not a crisis.

65
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:47,110
Apparently, I favored the left one,

66
00:03:47,110 --> 00:03:49,570
she got a little lopsided.

67
00:03:50,680 --> 00:03:54,080
Oh, my God, you still go left!

68
00:03:58,370 --> 00:04:01,020
Which celebrity would you say I look like the most?

69
00:04:01,020 --> 00:04:04,230
Halle Berry.

70
00:04:04,990 --> 00:04:05,970
Why?

71
00:04:05,970 --> 00:04:08,030
Stuart and I are putting dating profiles online,

72
00:04:08,030 --> 00:04:09,880
and it's one of the questions.

73
00:04:10,240 --> 00:04:13,990
And thank you-- I'd kill for that woman's bone structure.

74
00:04:15,390 --> 00:04:17,660
Why are you reading Pride and Prejudice?

75
00:04:17,660 --> 00:04:18,980
I'll tell you why.

76
00:04:18,980 --> 00:04:21,670
Amy ruined Raiders of the Lost Ark for me,

77
00:04:21,690 --> 00:04:22,790
so now I'm trying to find

78
00:04:22,790 --> 00:04:25,860
something beloved to her and ruin that.

79
00:04:27,380 --> 00:04:29,910
Because her life wasn't enough?

80
00:04:32,410 --> 00:04:33,560
Wait...

81
00:04:33,560 --> 00:04:35,760
how can, how can anyone ruin Raiders?

82
00:04:35,760 --> 00:04:36,630
It's perfect.

83
00:04:36,630 --> 00:04:38,700
Yeah, except for the fact that Indiana Jones

84
00:04:38,700 --> 00:04:41,920
is completely irrelevant to the story. With or without him,

85
00:04:41,920 --> 00:04:45,120
the Nazis find the ark, open it and die.

86
00:04:53,530 --> 00:04:54,110
Hey, wait a minute.

87
00:04:54,110 --> 00:04:57,020
No, the Nazis were digging in the wrong place.

88
00:04:57,020 --> 00:04:58,070
The only reason they got the ark

89
00:04:58,070 --> 00:04:59,730
was because Indy found it first.

90
00:04:59,730 --> 00:05:01,600
Actually, they were only digging in the wrong place

91
00:05:01,600 --> 00:05:02,920
because Indy had the medallion.

92
00:05:02,920 --> 00:05:04,340
Without him, they would have had the medallion

93
00:05:04,340 --> 00:05:07,180
and dug in the right place.

94
00:05:15,540 --> 00:05:16,830
Okay, I know you don't want to talk about it,

95
00:05:16,830 --> 00:05:19,680
but can I just ask you one question about your mom's book?

96
00:05:19,680 --> 00:05:21,220
No.

97
00:05:21,220 --> 00:05:22,160
I just want to know

98
00:05:22,160 --> 00:05:24,330
why a five-year-old boy puts on his mom's makeup

99
00:05:24,330 --> 00:05:26,800
and wears balloon boobies.

100
00:05:29,660 --> 00:05:32,870
They weren't boobies, they were muscles.

101
00:05:32,870 --> 00:05:34,130
And the makeup was green.

102
00:05:34,130 --> 00:05:37,280
I was pretending to be The Hulk.

103
00:05:37,280 --> 00:05:38,220
You were wearing her bra.

104
00:05:38,220 --> 00:05:39,490
That was to keep my muscles from sagging!

105
00:05:39,490 --> 00:05:41,950
Can we please stop talking about this?!

106
00:05:42,700 --> 00:05:44,020
Okay, okay.

107
00:05:44,020 --> 00:05:45,750
But you know, as a student of psychology

108
00:05:45,750 --> 00:05:49,260
who got a check-plus on her first homework assignment...

109
00:05:49,960 --> 00:05:51,720
I think, sometimes, it's good to

110
00:05:51,720 --> 00:05:53,310
open up about these things.

111
00:05:53,310 --> 00:05:54,310
Okay, fine.

112
00:05:54,310 --> 00:05:56,320
Do you want to know why I dressed like The Hulk?

113
00:05:56,320 --> 00:05:57,830
Because I was always mad at my mom

114
00:05:57,830 --> 00:06:00,690
and I wanted to smash my way out of that house.

115
00:06:00,690 --> 00:06:02,340
Well, why were you so angry?

116
00:06:02,340 --> 00:06:03,680
Gee, I don't know.

117
00:06:03,680 --> 00:06:06,920
Maybe it's because I was always the subject of her little experiments.

118
00:06:06,920 --> 00:06:09,700
Did you get to the chapter where she staged the Easter egg hunt

119
00:06:09,700 --> 00:06:12,630
with no eggs to see how long I'd keep looking?

120
00:06:14,060 --> 00:06:15,290
The answer, by the way:

121
00:06:15,290 --> 00:06:17,240
June.

122
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:20,000
Sweetie, I'm so sorry.

123
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:21,880
I wish there was something I could do to make you feel better.

124
00:06:21,880 --> 00:06:23,610
I do, too, but there's not.

125
00:06:23,610 --> 00:06:26,370
Really? Are you sure about that?

126
00:06:29,790 --> 00:06:32,620
Of course, who am I to argue with a check-plus student?

127
00:06:34,670 --> 00:06:35,790
Just warning you-- I'm gonna go right.

128
00:06:35,790 --> 00:06:38,250
Don't make a big deal out of it.

129
00:06:46,570 --> 00:06:49,380
Is makeup really necessary?

130
00:06:49,550 --> 00:06:51,100
Well, when someone looks at your dating profile,

131
00:06:51,100 --> 00:06:53,070
the first thing they see is your picture.

132
00:06:53,070 --> 00:06:54,830
I just want to make sure you look fun

133
00:06:54,830 --> 00:06:57,090
and full of life and not like a body

134
00:06:57,090 --> 00:06:59,110
they just pulled out of the river.

135
00:07:00,080 --> 00:07:03,200
All right, here we go, and...

136
00:07:03,200 --> 00:07:05,380
smile.

137
00:07:09,650 --> 00:07:12,230
Okay, uh-uh, that one's in the bank.

138
00:07:13,030 --> 00:07:14,480
How about this?

139
00:07:14,480 --> 00:07:16,490
Turn away, and then turn back into it.

140
00:07:16,490 --> 00:07:17,510
But when you do,

141
00:07:17,510 --> 00:07:21,180
imagine the camera is the girl you want to meet.

142
00:07:21,180 --> 00:07:22,950
You got it.

143
00:07:32,190 --> 00:07:33,510
Okay, uh,

144
00:07:33,510 --> 00:07:35,580
let's try it again.

145
00:07:35,580 --> 00:07:37,840
Uh, but this time, pretend the girl you want to meet

146
00:07:37,840 --> 00:07:39,940
doesn't want to hurt you.

147
00:07:41,670 --> 00:07:44,030
I don't think I can give you that.

148
00:07:44,030 --> 00:07:45,990
Come on. One more time.

149
00:07:55,630 --> 00:07:58,040
Yeah, it's, it's a little blurry,

150
00:07:58,040 --> 00:08:00,760
but I think that works in your favor.

151
00:08:00,760 --> 00:08:03,190
- Do you want a beer? - Sure.

152
00:08:03,190 --> 00:08:05,640
Hey, have you finished writing your profile yet?

153
00:08:05,640 --> 00:08:06,860
Almost.

154
00:08:06,860 --> 00:08:08,070
Oh, what did you put

155
00:08:08,070 --> 00:08:10,380
as the one-word description of yourself?

156
00:08:10,380 --> 00:08:13,230
I put unobjectionable.

157
00:08:13,230 --> 00:08:14,470
But now that I hear it out loud,

158
00:08:14,470 --> 00:08:17,440
it just seems like I'm being cocky.

159
00:08:17,440 --> 00:08:19,500
What did you put for your best feature?

160
00:08:19,500 --> 00:08:22,070
My parents' money.

161
00:08:23,590 --> 00:08:25,450
Uh, what did you put for your best feature?

162
00:08:25,450 --> 00:08:28,220
I put not applicable.

163
00:08:28,690 --> 00:08:30,940
Come on, dude, you're being too hard on yourself.

164
00:08:30,940 --> 00:08:32,620
You've got a lot of good stuff going on.

165
00:08:32,620 --> 00:08:33,950
Really? Like what?

166
00:08:33,950 --> 00:08:36,920
Well, okay, you're a, you're a talented artist,

167
00:08:36,920 --> 00:08:38,810
you own your own business.

168
00:08:38,810 --> 00:08:41,980
Neither of those things have ever helped me meet a woman.

169
00:08:41,980 --> 00:08:45,060
Okay, well, can we imply

170
00:08:45,060 --> 00:08:47,730
that you're well-endowed?

171
00:08:48,200 --> 00:08:53,110
I do have one oddly long testicle.

172
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:56,750
Okay, now you're talking like a winner!

173
00:09:00,500 --> 00:09:01,860
Whatcha doin'?

174
00:09:01,860 --> 00:09:04,900
Oh, it turns out Amy's beloved Pride and Prejudice

175
00:09:04,900 --> 00:09:07,470
is a flawless masterpiece.

176
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:09,470
He's got too much pride,

177
00:09:09,470 --> 00:09:10,840
she's got too much prejudice--

178
00:09:10,840 --> 00:09:13,010
it just works.

179
00:09:13,010 --> 00:09:14,770
So you're looking to ruin something for her

180
00:09:14,770 --> 00:09:16,200
in the funny pages?

181
00:09:16,200 --> 00:09:21,030
Amy has a fondness for the comic strip Marmaduke.

182
00:09:21,230 --> 00:09:22,060
And...?

183
00:09:22,060 --> 00:09:23,940
And I think I've got it.

184
00:09:23,940 --> 00:09:24,900
Consider:

185
00:09:24,900 --> 00:09:27,870
a family possesses a dog that is so large

186
00:09:27,870 --> 00:09:29,180
and poorly disciplined,

187
00:09:29,180 --> 00:09:31,620
he causes nothing but problems.

188
00:09:31,620 --> 00:09:33,340
Why do they keep him?!

189
00:09:35,390 --> 00:09:37,630
Maybe they fell in love with him as a puppy

190
00:09:37,630 --> 00:09:39,660
and didn't know how big he was gonna be.

191
00:09:39,660 --> 00:09:41,760
Of course.

192
00:09:42,190 --> 00:09:44,360
You know, why couldn't she just like Ziggy?

193
00:09:44,360 --> 00:09:45,270
Yeah?

194
00:09:45,270 --> 00:09:47,900
That thing's riddled with plot holes.

195
00:09:49,190 --> 00:09:50,110
Sorry, buddy.

196
00:09:50,960 --> 00:09:53,970
I think she's a fan of Garfield as well.

197
00:09:54,740 --> 00:09:57,800
Oh, darn it, now so am I.

198
00:09:57,880 --> 00:09:58,700
I'll see you later.

199
00:09:58,700 --> 00:10:01,090
I gotta go watch a stupid football game with Penny.

200
00:10:01,090 --> 00:10:02,490
Wait-- hang on.

201
00:10:02,490 --> 00:10:04,090
You've spent time with Amy.

202
00:10:04,090 --> 00:10:06,420
Can you think of anything she's fond of

203
00:10:06,420 --> 00:10:10,730
that has a bunch of flaws she hasn't noticed?

204
00:10:14,750 --> 00:10:16,660
I gotta go.

205
00:10:21,540 --> 00:10:23,210
- You ready to go? - Yep.

206
00:10:23,210 --> 00:10:24,300
Hey, and maybe this time

207
00:10:24,300 --> 00:10:27,390
you don't try and talk sports with the guys.

208
00:10:28,050 --> 00:10:29,230
Some sports bar.

209
00:10:29,230 --> 00:10:31,750
It's like they never even heard of Quidditch.

210
00:10:32,440 --> 00:10:33,570
Do we really have to go?

211
00:10:33,570 --> 00:10:34,720
Oh, come on. Every time we're about

212
00:10:34,720 --> 00:10:36,450
to hang out with my friends, you don't want to.

213
00:10:36,450 --> 00:10:37,710
It's like, "It's too loud,"

214
00:10:37,710 --> 00:10:39,240
or "the bathroom's too dirty,"

215
00:10:39,240 --> 00:10:42,310
or "they put a chicken wing in my ear..." I mean...

216
00:10:43,280 --> 00:10:44,200
Well, you're-you're right.

217
00:10:44,200 --> 00:10:45,160
Let's just go.

218
00:10:45,160 --> 00:10:46,420
Hey, what's going on with you?

219
00:10:46,420 --> 00:10:48,150
Nothing, I'm fine.

220
00:10:48,150 --> 00:10:49,200
All right, hang on.

221
00:10:49,200 --> 00:10:50,830
is this still about your mom's book?

222
00:10:50,830 --> 00:10:53,210
No. Not everything is about my mom.

223
00:10:53,210 --> 00:10:54,430
'Cause if you're still upset about that,

224
00:10:54,430 --> 00:10:55,460
we don't have to go.

225
00:10:55,460 --> 00:10:58,470
Except this is totally about my mom.

226
00:10:59,770 --> 00:11:00,900
I'm so sorry.

227
00:11:00,900 --> 00:11:02,180
I never should have read that book.

228
00:11:02,180 --> 00:11:03,620
You know what? You want to just get dinner

229
00:11:03,620 --> 00:11:04,530
and watch the game here?

230
00:11:05,260 --> 00:11:07,640
- That sounds nice. - Okay.

231
00:11:07,640 --> 00:11:09,400
Or, you know, we could get take-out

232
00:11:09,400 --> 00:11:10,820
and watch the Blu-ray extended version

233
00:11:10,820 --> 00:11:13,710
of The Hobbit movie with commentary track.

234
00:11:16,690 --> 00:11:19,780
On account of how sad I am about my mom.

235
00:11:25,460 --> 00:11:26,870
Leonard, you ready for lunch?

236
00:11:26,870 --> 00:11:28,840
One sec!

237
00:11:30,290 --> 00:11:31,900
Hey. Sorry.

238
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:36,130
- Hi, Penny. - Hi.

239
00:11:36,130 --> 00:11:36,910
All right, sweetie.

240
00:11:36,910 --> 00:11:38,610
You hang in there today.

241
00:11:38,610 --> 00:11:40,360
I'll try, but I might be sad again tonight.

242
00:11:40,360 --> 00:11:41,950
Okay.

243
00:11:45,540 --> 00:11:47,180
Sex at work?!

244
00:11:47,180 --> 00:11:48,530
Leave it alone.

245
00:11:48,530 --> 00:11:50,580
- That's my girlfriend. - Sorry.

246
00:11:50,580 --> 00:11:53,450
Who just had sex with me at work!

247
00:11:54,140 --> 00:11:55,730
Damn. How'd you swing that?

248
00:11:55,730 --> 00:11:58,250
Well, whenever I talk about how awful my mom was,

249
00:11:58,250 --> 00:12:00,620
Penny will do anything to make me feel better.

250
00:12:00,620 --> 00:12:01,720
- Seriously? - Look, I mean...

251
00:12:01,720 --> 00:12:05,390
I'm not proud of it, but it does work.

252
00:12:05,390 --> 00:12:06,250
I-I got her to watch

253
00:12:06,250 --> 00:12:10,310
a six-part documentary on Monty Python.

254
00:12:10,310 --> 00:12:11,740
Even I was bored, I just wanted to see

255
00:12:11,740 --> 00:12:14,000
if she'd make it to the end.

256
00:12:14,550 --> 00:12:15,580
You sound kind of proud of it.

257
00:12:15,580 --> 00:12:17,040
I am; I'm really proud.

258
00:12:20,170 --> 00:12:20,890
Hello, Sheldon.

259
00:12:20,890 --> 00:12:22,190
Is everything okay?

260
00:12:22,190 --> 00:12:23,330
Yes.

261
00:12:23,330 --> 00:12:24,190
Why?

262
00:12:24,190 --> 00:12:26,620
Well, the last time you made an unscheduled video-chat,

263
00:12:26,620 --> 00:12:28,440
there was a curly fry in your regular fries

264
00:12:28,440 --> 00:12:31,580
and you thought someone might be trying to slip you a mickey.

265
00:12:33,500 --> 00:12:35,080
April 13...

266
00:12:35,690 --> 00:12:38,170
a dark night, indeed.

267
00:12:39,110 --> 00:12:40,590
So what can I do for you?

268
00:12:40,590 --> 00:12:42,470
I'm calling to invite you

269
00:12:42,470 --> 00:12:45,260
to a spontaneous date night tomorrow evening.

270
00:12:45,260 --> 00:12:46,150
Really?

271
00:12:46,150 --> 00:12:47,360
Yes.

272
00:12:47,360 --> 00:12:48,480
You were kind enough

273
00:12:48,480 --> 00:12:50,720
to watch Raiders of the Lost Ark with me.

274
00:12:50,720 --> 00:12:52,900
So I'd like to return the favor

275
00:12:52,900 --> 00:12:54,850
by inviting you to watch an episode

276
00:12:54,850 --> 00:12:57,960
of your favorite childhood television series,

277
00:12:57,960 --> 00:13:00,430
Little House on the Prairie.

278
00:13:02,060 --> 00:13:03,970
That sounds lovely.

279
00:13:04,370 --> 00:13:07,100
Why are you rubbing your hands together?

280
00:13:10,510 --> 00:13:11,500
I'm putting on lotion.

281
00:13:11,500 --> 00:13:13,200
Are you in or not?

282
00:13:13,680 --> 00:13:15,140
Of course I'm in.

283
00:13:15,140 --> 00:13:16,120
Excellent.

284
00:13:16,120 --> 00:13:17,850
Then I shall see you tomorrow.

285
00:13:17,850 --> 00:13:19,430
Good night, Dr. Fowler.

286
00:13:19,430 --> 00:13:20,940
Good night, Dr. Cooper.

287
00:13:21,610 --> 00:13:24,420
Good night, indeed.

288
00:13:25,290 --> 00:13:26,610
What a rube.

289
00:13:26,610 --> 00:13:30,380
Why would I put on lotion when I have such soft hands?

290
00:13:31,840 --> 00:13:33,160
You were really quiet during dinner.

291
00:13:33,160 --> 00:13:34,590
Is everything okay?

292
00:13:34,590 --> 00:13:35,200
Yeah.

293
00:13:35,200 --> 00:13:37,570
I guess I was just thinking about my mom,

294
00:13:37,570 --> 00:13:40,870
and how sad my childhood was.

295
00:13:42,390 --> 00:13:43,590
Yeah, I bet it sucked.

296
00:13:43,590 --> 00:13:45,730
I'm gonna take a bath; you do the dishes.

297
00:13:45,730 --> 00:13:48,320
How about I take a bath with you

298
00:13:48,320 --> 00:13:50,540
and see what happens.

299
00:13:50,540 --> 00:13:52,000
Here's what's gonna happen:

300
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:52,930
I'm gonna take a bath,

301
00:13:52,930 --> 00:13:54,720
and you're gonna do the dishes.

302
00:13:54,720 --> 00:13:55,460
That's it?

303
00:13:55,460 --> 00:13:57,320
No compassion?

304
00:13:57,320 --> 00:13:58,500
Aw, poor Howie.

305
00:13:58,500 --> 00:14:00,530
We good? I'm gonna take a bath.

306
00:14:00,530 --> 00:14:01,670
Bernie...

307
00:14:01,670 --> 00:14:04,130
God, what is going on with you?

308
00:14:04,670 --> 00:14:06,740
I'm sharing my pain.

309
00:14:07,440 --> 00:14:10,620
And I'm not buying it. Try again.

310
00:14:11,490 --> 00:14:14,500
I'm learning to be a man in a culture

311
00:14:14,500 --> 00:14:17,410
where it's increasingly difficult to know how...?

312
00:14:17,410 --> 00:14:20,290
Strike two.

313
00:14:20,930 --> 00:14:22,080
I'm copying Leonard.

314
00:14:22,080 --> 00:14:23,060
When he does this to Penny,

315
00:14:23,060 --> 00:14:25,530
they have sex and watch Monty Python.

316
00:14:26,110 --> 00:14:26,610
- Howard! - I know.

317
00:14:26,610 --> 00:14:27,450
It was dumb,

318
00:14:27,450 --> 00:14:28,210
I shouldn't have done it.

319
00:14:28,210 --> 00:14:30,780
And it's making me feel sad...

320
00:14:31,720 --> 00:14:33,980
So sad.

321
00:14:35,920 --> 00:14:38,480
You know, why don't you take a bath? I'll do the dishes.

322
00:14:41,890 --> 00:14:45,040
Three, two, one...

323
00:14:45,490 --> 00:14:46,630
That's it.

324
00:14:46,630 --> 00:14:49,400
Our dating profiles are live on the Internet.

325
00:14:49,400 --> 00:14:50,930
Attention all shoppers:

326
00:14:50,930 --> 00:14:54,760
my business is open for business!

327
00:14:55,570 --> 00:14:57,310
That's right, ladies.

328
00:14:57,310 --> 00:14:58,550
For all you know,

329
00:14:58,550 --> 00:15:01,970
I'm confident and fun to be around.

330
00:15:04,630 --> 00:15:05,990
Oh, cool, it tells you

331
00:15:05,990 --> 00:15:08,140
when someone's reading your profile.

332
00:15:08,140 --> 00:15:11,410
"Jenny309."

333
00:15:11,410 --> 00:15:13,820
I hope that's not her weight.

334
00:15:14,760 --> 00:15:16,830
If it is, I'll... I'll take her.

335
00:15:18,120 --> 00:15:18,920
Good one.

336
00:15:20,800 --> 00:15:23,050
Ooh, I got one, too.

337
00:15:23,050 --> 00:15:26,170
The ladies are coming to us.

338
00:15:26,980 --> 00:15:29,030
Oh, man, if I'd started this years ago,

339
00:15:29,030 --> 00:15:31,830
I'd be divorced two or three times by now.

340
00:15:33,300 --> 00:15:35,450
What...? Another one.

341
00:15:35,450 --> 00:15:37,170
You know, it... it's weird.

342
00:15:37,170 --> 00:15:38,850
When they're reading your profile, does it...

343
00:15:38,850 --> 00:15:40,690
does it make you feel exposed?

344
00:15:40,690 --> 00:15:42,850
Like they see you naked?

345
00:15:44,040 --> 00:15:47,180
Well, they're not running away screaming, so, no.

346
00:15:49,660 --> 00:15:51,280
I love Little House.

347
00:15:51,280 --> 00:15:53,010
It made me want to live on a farm so much

348
00:15:53,010 --> 00:15:55,230
I tried to milk my cat.

349
00:15:58,640 --> 00:15:59,920
That tangy bowl of Cheerios

350
00:15:59,920 --> 00:16:01,810
was not worth the stitches.

351
00:16:03,070 --> 00:16:05,740
Well, you sit back, relax

352
00:16:05,740 --> 00:16:09,340
and enjoy a beloved childhood memory.

353
00:16:13,160 --> 00:16:15,220
You see that cabin there?

354
00:16:15,220 --> 00:16:19,420
I read they were illegally squatting on Indian land.

355
00:16:20,660 --> 00:16:21,200
Yeah.

356
00:16:21,200 --> 00:16:23,040
Personally, I think what we did

357
00:16:23,040 --> 00:16:25,240
to the Native Americans was wrong,

358
00:16:25,240 --> 00:16:28,740
but this is your favorite show, not mine.

359
00:16:28,740 --> 00:16:31,150
Oh, look at little Laura Ingalls,

360
00:16:31,150 --> 00:16:33,380
eating that peanut butter sandwich.

361
00:16:33,840 --> 00:16:35,240
Peanut butter?!

362
00:16:37,800 --> 00:16:40,110
That's strange, since peanut butter

363
00:16:40,110 --> 00:16:43,650
wasn't introduced until the early 1900s.

364
00:16:45,660 --> 00:16:47,570
If I knew this show was about time travel,

365
00:16:47,570 --> 00:16:50,340
I would have watched it much sooner.

366
00:16:53,490 --> 00:16:54,600
You're trying to get back at me

367
00:16:54,600 --> 00:16:56,570
for what I said about Raiders of the Lost Ark.

368
00:16:56,570 --> 00:16:58,290
That's silly.

369
00:16:58,290 --> 00:17:01,020
Almost as silly as Dr. Baker having a telephone,

370
00:17:01,020 --> 00:17:02,220
since telephones only existed

371
00:17:02,220 --> 00:17:04,770
in large cities at that time.

372
00:17:04,770 --> 00:17:07,600
This is more like Little House on the Preposterous.

373
00:17:09,060 --> 00:17:11,550
Sheldon, we're in a relationship.

374
00:17:11,550 --> 00:17:14,130
When you get angry, just tell me.

375
00:17:14,130 --> 00:17:16,410
You don't need to seek revenge.

376
00:17:16,410 --> 00:17:18,310
Are you sure?

377
00:17:19,460 --> 00:17:21,110
Every time my dad stayed out all night,

378
00:17:21,110 --> 00:17:24,780
my mom would put hamster poop in his chewing tobacco.

379
00:17:26,500 --> 00:17:28,650
Well, that's not how we're going to do it.

380
00:17:28,650 --> 00:17:30,300
Fine.

381
00:17:30,300 --> 00:17:32,080
I'm mad at you.

382
00:17:32,080 --> 00:17:34,110
Not only did you ruin Raiders for me,

383
00:17:34,110 --> 00:17:36,680
you may have ruined the whole franchise.

384
00:17:36,680 --> 00:17:38,100
Except for the fourth one,

385
00:17:38,100 --> 00:17:40,930
which was bad before you got your mitts on it.

386
00:17:42,040 --> 00:17:43,370
I-I shouldn't have said it.

387
00:17:43,370 --> 00:17:44,930
I'm sorry.

388
00:17:44,930 --> 00:17:46,630
Thank you.

389
00:17:46,630 --> 00:17:47,760
Do you feel better?

390
00:17:47,760 --> 00:17:49,270
Yes.

391
00:17:49,270 --> 00:17:50,870
But not as good as I'm going to when I tell you

392
00:17:50,870 --> 00:17:54,700
that your precious Garfield has no reason to hate Mondays.

393
00:17:55,450 --> 00:17:57,910
He's a cat. He doesn't have a job.

394
00:18:03,010 --> 00:18:06,080
Hey, I was just-- what is happening?

395
00:18:07,280 --> 00:18:08,880
Oh, just a little treat.

396
00:18:08,880 --> 00:18:10,410
I know you've been feeling really bad

397
00:18:10,410 --> 00:18:12,210
about your mom lately.

398
00:18:12,210 --> 00:18:13,590
Oh, oh, I have.

399
00:18:13,590 --> 00:18:15,060
So bad.

400
00:18:15,660 --> 00:18:17,380
And I wanted to make you feel better,

401
00:18:17,380 --> 00:18:20,410
so I planned something very special for you.

402
00:18:20,760 --> 00:18:23,090
I can already feel it working.

403
00:18:25,040 --> 00:18:27,510
Hello, Leonard.

404
00:18:30,130 --> 00:18:31,220
Mom?!

405
00:18:31,220 --> 00:18:34,480
I understand you have been whining about my parenting

406
00:18:34,480 --> 00:18:37,360
in order to emotionally manipulate your girlfriend.

407
00:18:37,360 --> 00:18:38,880
I... uh...

408
00:18:38,880 --> 00:18:40,330
Bernadette told me everything.

409
00:18:40,330 --> 00:18:43,090
Now you don't get the left or the right.

410
00:18:45,390 --> 00:18:48,200
Let's discuss why you continue to involve me

411
00:18:48,200 --> 00:18:49,550
in your sex life.

412
00:18:49,760 --> 00:18:50,440
Oh, please, Mommy.

413
00:18:50,440 --> 00:18:52,100
No, Mommy.

414
00:18:53,150 --> 00:18:54,330
When you were six years old,

415
00:18:54,330 --> 00:18:57,950
you walked in on me and your father naked.

416
00:18:58,560 --> 00:19:00,160
I was swatting his bottom

417
00:19:00,160 --> 00:19:03,560
with your brand new Ping Pong paddle.

418
00:19:05,950 --> 00:19:08,640
I didn't dream that?

419
00:19:09,850 --> 00:19:12,420
How did that make you feel?

420
00:19:13,230 --> 00:19:14,020
Penny, come back!

421
00:19:14,020 --> 00:19:16,240
I'm sad for real now!

422
00:19:17,980 --> 00:19:19,310
In the last two hours,

423
00:19:19,310 --> 00:19:22,470
162 women have read our profiles.

424
00:19:22,470 --> 00:19:24,220
How many of them have sent us messages?

425
00:19:24,220 --> 00:19:25,960
- Combined? - Yes.

426
00:19:25,960 --> 00:19:27,580
Zero.

427
00:19:29,790 --> 00:19:31,760
Dude, this is... this is brutal.

428
00:19:31,760 --> 00:19:34,620
I don't think I've ever felt so rejected.

429
00:19:34,620 --> 00:19:36,500
And I had a rescue dog

430
00:19:36,500 --> 00:19:38,980
who ran back to the pound.

431
00:19:41,440 --> 00:19:42,440
This is the worst.

432
00:19:42,440 --> 00:19:43,500
If we're gonna get shot down,

433
00:19:43,500 --> 00:19:45,440
we might as well just go to a bar

434
00:19:45,440 --> 00:19:46,440
and do it old school.

435
00:19:46,440 --> 00:19:48,280
And make them look us in the eye.

436
00:19:48,280 --> 00:19:50,470
Yeah, anything is better than this.

437
00:19:50,470 --> 00:19:51,900
Hello.

438
00:19:52,090 --> 00:19:53,660
Not interested.

439
00:19:55,790 --> 00:19:57,740
I was wrong. This is worse.

440
00:20:07,020 --> 00:20:09,360
Wait, wait-- if it wasn't for Indiana Jones,

441
00:20:09,360 --> 00:20:11,650
the ark would never have ended up at the warehouse!

442
00:20:11,650 --> 00:20:13,160
That's true!

443
00:20:13,160 --> 00:20:15,340
He collected and delivered the ark

444
00:20:15,340 --> 00:20:17,400
to the proper authorities for filing.

445
00:20:17,400 --> 00:20:18,400
Like a hero!

446
00:20:18,400 --> 00:20:20,560
- Yeah! Yes! - Right!

447
00:20:22,340 --> 00:20:23,300
Although, technically,

448
00:20:23,300 --> 00:20:24,760
Indy was supposed to take the ark

449
00:20:24,760 --> 00:20:25,660
to a museum to be studied.

450
00:20:25,660 --> 00:20:28,180
He couldn't even get that done.

